To include the STOR (store a file) and RETR (retrieve a file) client requests in the proper locations, we can assume a typical sequence of operations where a file is uploaded after connecting and before listing files, and a file is downloaded after listing files. Here’s how the modified sequence of client requests could look:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
STOR filename.txt   ; (This is where we upload a file)
RETR filename.txt   ; (This is where we retrieve a file)
LIST
QUIT
```

In this modified sequence, `STOR filename.txt` is added after the `PORT` command to indicate that the client wants to upload a file named `filename.txt`. The `RETR filename.txt` command is added after the `STOR` command to indicate that the client wants to retrieve the same file after listing the files on the server. You can replace `filename.txt` with the actual file name you intend to upload or retrieve

